    "reason": "[ev-fa371709f05a] says only that Istio no longer writes a kubeconfig to the CNI net directory. That gives a subject and a change type (removed), but it doesn't say which component read that kubeconfig or which setups relied on it, so applicability can't be written. It also doesn't say what fails for an operator who does nothing, so there's no consequence. The nearby note [ev-191d17c9702d] says `CNI_NET_DIR` was dropped from the istio-cni configmap because it now does nothing, which suggests the two changes are linked, but it doesn't name who is exposed or what breaks either. We need the PR, upgrade-guide text or a notes entry that names the consumers of that kubeconfig and the impact on them.",
